The headers under include/ stand in for the Linux kernel headers that amdgpu's
display code includes, so that it compiles as a host program. They are not
Linux code. They come from tools/dcn41/linuxshim of Navi48-MacOS
(https://github.com/Almosst-DEV/Navi48-MacOS, export of 2026-10-02), with
these changes: linux/slab.h gained kzalloc_objs, kmalloc_objs, kvzalloc_obj
and kvmalloc_obj; linux/device.h is new; drm/display/drm_dp_helper.h now
includes Linux's drm_dp.h; the placeholder ObjectID.h,
atomfirmwareid.h, atom.h and amdgpu.h were dropped in favour of the real
headers.

